# ctrl-b environment — copy to `.env` (gitignored). Everything here is OPTIONAL.
#
# Secrets model is HYBRID (docs/DESIGN.md §9):
#   • config.yaml  = the UI-managed source of truth, and the ONLY home for secrets
#                    (per-host SSH creds, per-provider API keys). 0600, gitignored;
#                    the Conf tab edits it.
#   • .env (this)  = bootstrap/deploy knobs + overrides for DECLARED, ONE-LEVEL SCALARS.
#                    It cannot reach a provider credential — those live at
#                    providers.<name>.api_key, two levels down — and structured config
#                    (host lists, MCP servers) is not settable here either.
#                    A variable naming a path the schema doesn't declare is LOGGED as
#                    ineffective at startup; one naming a path a config migration retired
#                    makes `python -m app.config_migration --check` refuse.
#
# Real shell environment variables always take precedence over values in this file.

# --- bootstrap paths (where the app reads config / writes the db) ---
# CTRLB_CONFIG=C:\path\to\config.yaml      # default: repo-root config.yaml
# CTRLB_DB=C:\path\to\ctrlb.db             # default: repo-root ctrlb.db
# CTRLB_ENV=C:\path\to\.env                # default: repo-root .env

# --- config overrides: CTRLB_<SECTION>__<KEY> overrides config.yaml's <section>.<key> ---
# Note the DOUBLE underscore between section and key. Scalars only.
# CTRLB_SERVER__HOST=127.0.0.1
# CTRLB_SERVER__PORT=5433
# CTRLB_SERVER__DEBUG=false
# CTRLB_SERVER__POLL_SECONDS=5

# --- NOT settable here: secrets ---
# There is deliberately no way to supply an API key from this file. Earlier revisions of this
# example advertised CTRLB_INFERENCE__CLOUD_KEY / CTRLB_STT__KEY / CTRLB_TTS__KEY /
# CTRLB_EMBEDDINGS__KEY — none of those ever named a real field, so they silently did nothing.
# Put the key in config.yaml (Conf tab → Providers), which is 0600 and gitignored.
